{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Danger: Man At Work – In the Balance|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1969|09|24}} |ProdCode=01 |ShortSummary=
:Part one of a six-part series on pollution. By means of film, interviews and comments by experts, the programs show how we are polluting soil, air and water; what is being done about the problem; and what our chances are for survival. With host John Livingston.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=Fr8DH2VBP9sC&dat=19690924&printsec=frontpage&hl=en |title=Today's TV Previews |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=September 24, 1969 |page=49 |access-date=April 28, 2016 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123652/https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=Fr8DH2VBP9sC&dat=19690924&printsec=frontpage&hl=en |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=Fr8DH2VBP9sC&dat=19690924&printsec=frontpage&hl=en |title=CBC-TV: The Nature of Things – Danger: Man At Work |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=September 24, 1969 |page=49 |access-date=April 28, 2016 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123652/https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=Fr8DH2VBP9sC&dat=19690924&printsec=frontpage&hl=en |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Danger: Man At Work – The Urban Crisis|OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|10|01}} |ProdCode=02 |ShortSummary=
:The ways man has succeeded and failed in duplicating in his cities the checks and balances of the natural environment.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46497551/ |title=CBOT Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=September 27, 1969 |page=8, The TV Journal |access-date=June 19, 2016 |archive-date=August 13, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813142514/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46497551/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Danger: Man At Work – Water|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1969|10|08}} |ProdCode=03 |ShortSummary=
:The third program in this series about the problem of pollution. Narrator John Livingston shows how water is distributed throughout our environment, how it purifies itself, and how man has maltreated it.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42986071/ |title=CBOT Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=October 4, 1969 |page=8, The TV Journal |access-date=December 12, 2016 |archive-date=December 20, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161220144026/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42986071/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Danger: Man At Work – Air Pollution |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|10|15}} |ProdCode=04 |ShortSummary=
:The thin layer of our atmosphere is renewed and kept in balance by two delicate cycles, dependent on living green plants. Pollution is destroying the green things which renew it.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42992498/ |title=Television Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=October 15, 1969 |page=58 |access-date=June 20, 2016 |archive-date=August 13, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813172203/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42992498/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Danger: Man At Work – Pesticides|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1969|10|22}} |ProdCode=05 |ShortSummary=
:This program investigates the long-term effects of pesticides such as DDT.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42997214/ |title=Television Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=October 22, 1969 |page=62 |access-date=June 21, 2016 |archive-date=August 14, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160814021902/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42997214/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Danger: Man At Work – The Global Crisis |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|10|29}} |ProdCode=06 |ShortSummary=
:The final program in this series presents statements and observation of experts on the extent of pollution, what the future may be, and what can be done to stop pollution of the environment.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/43001125/ |title=Television Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=October 29, 1969 |page=64 |access-date=June 20, 2016 |archive-date=August 13, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813190222/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/43001125/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=The Ages of Man: A Day in the Life of a G.P."; alternate title: "The Family Doctor |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|11|05}} |ProdCode=07 |ShortSummary=
:First of ten programs looking at Canada's achievements in medical research in the past decade. Cameras follow a young family physician (a general practitioner) through a busy day with patients at his office and at South Peel Hospital in Toronto. The film is also an examination of the direction medical training and health services are taking in Canada.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/44417823/ |title=Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=November 1, 1969 |page=8, The TV Journal |access-date=June 6, 2016 |archive-date=August 5, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160805132402/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/44417823/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Sg0uAAAAIBAJ&pg=2597%2C1036418 |title=Today's TV Previews |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=November 5, 1969 |page=24 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123648/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Sg0uAAAAIBAJ&pg=2597,1036418 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: A Breath of Life |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|11|12}} |ProdCode=08 |ShortSummary=
:Program about genetic defects that can be inherited. Dr. D. N. Crozier of Toronto's Hospital for Sick Children is a guest.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Tg0uAAAAIBAJ&pg=1019%2C2716008 |title=Today's TV Previews |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=November 12, 1969 |page=13 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123644/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Tg0uAAAAIBAJ&pg=1019,2716008 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}
