{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: The Attack on Cancer |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|11|26}} |ProdCode=09 |ShortSummary=
:This program centres on the exciting research into the effects of drugs on tumors in mice being conducted by the internationally renowned cancer research team at Toronto's [[Princess Margaret Cancer Centre|Princess Margaret Hospital]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/44426189/ |title=Television Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=November 26, 1969 |page=44 |access-date=June 21, 2016 |archive-date=August 14, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160814081855/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/44426189/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}
<!-- -->
<!-- No episode during the regular slot on 12/03/1969; musical-comedy special instead -->

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: Drugs |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|12|10}} |ProdCode=10 |ShortSummary=
:A study of how medical researchers are using animals to determine the effect of drugs such as marijuana and LSD, and even liquor, on man.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=mPwtAAAAIBAJ&pg=5078%2C1567477 |title=HIGHLIGHTS This Week |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=December 6, 1969 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123654/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=mPwtAAAAIBAJ&pg=5078,1567477 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46157098/ |title=Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=December 6, 1969 |page=8, The TV Journal |access-date=June 6, 2016 |archive-date=August 5, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160805132252/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46157098/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: The Cell |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1969|12|17}} |ProdCode=11 |ShortSummary=
: This program explains why it is essential to understand the complicated mechanism of the normal cell before we can really understand what happens when cancerous cells run out of control.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=LO4yAAAAIBAJ&pg=1810%2C4740717 |title=TV &#124; Times |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=December 13, 1969 |page=Wed. / Dec. 17 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123703/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=LO4yAAAAIBAJ&pg=1810,4740717 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: Arthritis|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1969|12|24}} |ProdCode=12 |ShortSummary=
:One quarter of all Canadians will be affected some time in their lives by arthritis. This program looks at a case of rheumatoid, the drug treatments available, and some of the therapeutic aids to assist a person suffering from the disease.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=hqIyAAAAIBAJ&pg=2272%2C2217098 |title=Wed. / Dec. 24 night |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=December 20, 1969 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123701/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=hqIyAAAAIBAJ&pg=2272,2217098 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: Decade Science Review"; alternate title: "Science Decade|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1969|12|31}} |ProdCode=13 |ShortSummary=
:This program is a brief review of the main achievements of science over the past ten years, and attempts to anticipate some of the advancements which may be expected in the seventies.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=jKIyAAAAIBAJ&pg=633%2C4360573 |title=Highlights tonight |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=December 31, 1969 |page=13 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123646/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=jKIyAAAAIBAJ&pg=633,4360573 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: Heart Disease|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|01|07}} |ProdCode=14 |ShortSummary=
:A look at the coronary thrombosis which kills three out of ten adults; heart research in Canada.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=NnoyAAAAIBAJ&pg=1761%2C626864 |title=Wed. / Jan. 7 |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=January 3, 1970}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: Transplants|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|01|15}} |ProdCode=15 |ShortSummary=
:History and research in the field of organ transplants.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98862742/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=January 11, 1970 |page=18-D |access-date=June 7, 2016 |archive-date=August 5, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160805161030/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98862742/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Ages of Man: A Definition of Death |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1970|01|22}} |ProdCode=16 |ShortSummary=
:When is a man dead? Canadian physicians discuss the medical, ethical and legal questions involved with death, organ transplants and maintaining physical life after the death of the brain. (Last of the series).<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98902227/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=January 18, 1970 |page=22-D |access-date=June 9, 2016 |archive-date=August 7, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160807011738/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98902227/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=[[Wild Africa (film)|Wild Africa: As It Was]] |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1970|02|25}} |ProdCode=special |ShortSummary=
:The first of two programs depicting what remains of Africa's wildlife. This special features wild animals as they are protected and encouraged in Africa's national parks, including [[Queen Elizabeth National Park]], Uganda, the [[Amboseli National Park|Maasai Amboseli Game Reserve]], Kenya, the [[Ngorongoro Conservation Area|Ngorongoro Crater Conservation Area]] and Tanzania's [[Serengeti National Park]]. Film segments include a female cheetah tracking down her antelope prey; never-before-filmed scenes of the [[Egyptian vulture]] using rocks to break open other birds' eggs; and the daytime routine of a lion family.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98889376/ |title=Free Press Spotlight |work=Detroit Free Press |date=February 22, 1970 |page=19-D |access-date=December 1, 2016 |archive-date=December 1, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161201081237/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98889376/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}
<!-- ref indicating "Nature of Things" series: https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/210198238/ -->

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=A Sense of Time (Part 1)|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|03|19}} |ProdCode=17 |ShortSummary=
:First in a three-part series visiting some of Canada's 700 museums in an attempt to show how people of all ages use them for self-discovery, a sense of communication with the past and a greater awareness of what has shaped today's world.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98890825/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=March 15, 1970 |page=21-D |access-date=June 6, 2016 |archive-date=August 5, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160805123555/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98890825/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=[[Wild Africa (film)|Wild Africa: Something New]] |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1970|03|25}} |ProdCode=special |ShortSummary=
:Part two of a two-part special on Wild Africa. Today, wild Africa is in peril. Mushrooming human populations demand more and more of the ancient, easily violated landscape. Wild animals are on the retreat. Their last refuge is the magnificent system of national park and natural preserves. It is here that ecologists have established their field laboratories, to study the interrelationships of flora and fauna.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42810390/ |title=Wednesday |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=March 21, 1970 |page=8, The TV Journal |access-date=December 1, 2016 |archive-date=December 1, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161201210902/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/42810390/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=A Sense of Time (Part 2)|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|03|26}} |ProdCode=18 |ShortSummary=
:Second in a series of three programs on Canada's museums. This program presents views from adults – those who feel that the past has no relevance to their lives, and others who find themselves culturally enriched by the past. Includes a visit to the Royal Ontario Museum.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98891287/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=March 22, 1970 |page=22-D |access-date=June 8, 2016 |archive-date=August 6, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160806081651/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98891287/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=6cQtAAAAIBAJ&pg=1767%2C1869562 |title=TV Times |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=March 21, 1970 |page=Thu. / Mar. 26 night |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123644/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=6cQtAAAAIBAJ&pg=1767,1869562 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=A Sense of Time (Part 3)|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|04|02}} |ProdCode=19 |ShortSummary=
:A look "backstage" at the Ontario Science Center, the Royal Ontario Museum and Old Fort Henry.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98891693/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=March 29, 1970 |page=21-D |access-date=June 9, 2016 |archive-date=August 6, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160806233732/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98891693/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Oceanography|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|05|14}} |ProdCode=20 |ShortSummary=
:Recent advances in oceanography.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98904892/ |title=Tonight's Television Programs |work=Detroit Free Press |date=May 14, 1970 |access-date=December 2, 2016 |archive-date=December 2, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161202172522/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98904892/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}
<!-- 8:30 pm https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=b3oyAAAAIBAJ&sjid=JrkFAAAAIBAJ&pg=3424%2C1856329 -->

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Continental Drift|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|05|21}} |ProdCode=21 |ShortSummary=
:The theory that the Earth's continents are moving is examined.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=d3oyAAAAIBAJ&pg=2214%2C4397461 |title=TV Times |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=May 16, 1970 |page=27 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123703/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=d3oyAAAAIBAJ&pg=2214,4397461 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Sense Substitution|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|05|28}} |ProdCode=22 |ShortSummary=
:Research on new electronics and mechanical devices to help the blind and deaf realize true sensory perception.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98908791/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=May 24, 1970 |page=25-D |access-date=June 10, 2016 |archive-date=August 7, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160807194350/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98908791/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Physical Sciences: Stellar Evolution|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|06|04}} |ProdCode=23 |ShortSummary=
:The latest observations of astronomers have turned up new kinds of stars; mysterious emanations from deep in space called pulsars and quasars.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/43253868/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=May 30, 1970 |page=32 |access-date=June 10, 2016 |archive-date=August 8, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160808055315/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/43253868/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Physical Sciences: Making Waves|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|06|11}} |ProdCode=24 |ShortSummary=
:Research into the physics of sound and hearing has caused increasing alarm among scientists and physicians about the effects of high noise levels upon people, and the destructive psychological and physical effects of constant noise pollution.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41491086/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=June 6, 1970 |page=32 |access-date=June 10, 2016 |archive-date=August 8, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160808074635/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41491086/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Physical Sciences: Energy Conversion|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|06|18}} |ProdCode=25 |ShortSummary=
:The physics of energy and the problem of producing large quantities of energy with little pollution form the basis of this program.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41491470/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=June 13, 1970 |page=32 |access-date=June 11, 2016 |archive-date=August 8, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160808085507/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41491470/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Physical Sciences: Laser|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1970|06|25}} |ProdCode=26 |ShortSummary=
:The qualities of laser and normal light are contrasted. Final program in the series.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98913540/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=June 21, 1970 |page=25-D |access-date=June 11, 2016 |archive-date=August 8, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160808101418/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98913540/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41491863/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=June 20, 1970 |page=32 |access-date=June 11, 2016 |archive-date=August 8, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160808090940/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41491863/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

