{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Banting, Best and Insulin |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|10|04}} |ProdCode=01 |ShortSummary=
:Season opener: The Nature of Things looks at the discovery of insulin by [[Frederick Banting|Dr. Frederick Banting]] and [[Charles Best (medical scientist)|Dr. Charles Best]] and deals with the current Canadian research into diabetes.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Peacock |first=Bruce |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=VJ1ZAAAAIBAJ&pg=841%2C473816 |title=Tube Talk |work=The Leader-Post |location=Regina, Saskatchewan |date=October 4, 1971 |page=7 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123658/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=VJ1ZAAAAIBAJ&pg=841,473816 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99000736/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=October 3, 1971 |page=17-D |access-date=June 3, 2016 |archive-date=August 4, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160804152942/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99000736/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Cancer in Canada |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|10|11}} |ProdCode=02 |ShortSummary=
:Chances of recovery by a cancer patient in Canada are examined. Guests: [[James Till|Dr. James Till]], Toronto's Princess Margaret Hospital, and Dr. Robert Taylor of the National Cancer Institute.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99001948/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=October 10, 1971 |access-date=June 2, 2016 |archive-date=August 4, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160804133910/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99001948/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Population: Everybody's Baby |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|10|18}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:A visual exploration of the most difficult and serious issue threatening mankind today: the population crisis.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46161236/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=October 16, 1971 |page=19 |access-date=June 16, 2016 |archive-date=August 12, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160812203804/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46161236/ |url-status=live }}</ref> }}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Parkinsonism |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|10|25}} |ProdCode=03 |ShortSummary=
:A look at research which may bring hope to sufferers of a crippling disorder that affects those on the older side of the generation gap. Guests include Dr. [[Oleh Hornykiewicz]], a pioneer in the discovery of the drug [[L-DOPA]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99219732/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=October 24, 1971 |page=16-D |access-date=June 17, 2016 |archive-date=August 12, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160812210120/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99219732/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Rocky Mountains |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|11|01}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:The beautiful, vast tracts of land in the western mountain parks of the west coast and the Rocky Mountains are gradually being destroyed by camp sites, roads and towns. As they are opened their animal life gradually disappears.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=zroyAAAAIBAJ&pg=1102%2C136147 |title=TV highlights |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=November 1, 1971 |page=24 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123659/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=zroyAAAAIBAJ&pg=1102,136147 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Last Stand: The Everglades of Florida |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|11|15}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:An almost unique wildlife reserve is threatened by land developments and drainage policies.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=November 14, 1971 |page=15-D |url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99003607/ |access-date=June 17, 2016 |archive-date=August 13, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813060825/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99003607/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Last Stand: Point Pelee |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|11|22}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:Visit to Canada's last stronghold of the southern deciduous forest, a freshwater haven teeming with wildlife. But will it last?<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99219428/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=November 21, 1971 |page=16-D |access-date=June 17, 2016 |archive-date=August 13, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813053232/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99219428/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Living Arctic |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|11|29}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:''The Nature of Things'' presents the first part of its highly acclaimed White Paper special on the vast Arctic regions of Canada.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46168628/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=November 27, 1971 |page=19 |access-date=June 3, 2016 |archive-date=August 4, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160804153938/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46168628/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Last Stand: The Southwestern Desert |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|12|06}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:Last in a four-part series visits the U.S. Sonoran Desert, a prime example of plant and animal adaptation to a dry, harsh environment, where competition is keen and only the hardiest survive.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99010926/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=December 5, 1971 |page=13-D |access-date=June 18, 2016 |archive-date=August 13, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813103112/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99010926/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Fur Trade"; alternate title: "The Skin Trade |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|12|13}} |ProdCode=04 |ShortSummary=
:A look at the endangered species of animals used in the fur trade, focusing on the Canadian market.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99014711/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=December 12, 1971 |page=13-D |access-date=July 1, 2016 |archive-date=August 17, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160817131529/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99014711/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Population: Everybody's Baby |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1971|12|20}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
