{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Vanishing Peoples: Yanomami |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1972|01|31}} |ProdCode=09 |ShortSummary=
:Documentary look at the [[Yanomami]], a fast-vanishing Indian tribe inhabiting the tropical rainforest of the Upper [[Orinoco]] River in southeastern Venezuela and Northern Brazil.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99105296/ |title=TV Channels |work=Detroit Free Press |date=January 30, 1972 |page=13-D |access-date=July 2, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818130748/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99105296/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Insulin (repeat from 10/04/1971) |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1972|04|24}} |ProdCode=repeat}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Cancer in Canada |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1972|05|01}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:Canada is recognized as a world leader in cancer research, with its pioneer work in radiation therapy, the cobalt bomb and chemotherapy. Tonight's program examines the chances for recovery a cancer patient now has in Canada.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=JTg0AAAAIBAJ&pg=2663%2C4626940 |title=MON. / MAY 1 night |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=April 29, 1972 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123656/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=JTg0AAAAIBAJ&pg=2663,4626940 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Parkinson's Disease |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1972|05|08}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:Medical science does not yet know the exact causes of this disease but modern research into this crippling incapacitator of the middle-aged has resulted in improved treatment. This program offers a look at the disease and the treatment, with surgery and drugs, notably L-Dopa, giving many sufferers new hope.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=rLoyAAAAIBAJ&pg=1118%2C2513111 |title=TV highlights |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=May 8, 1972 |page=20 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123700/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=rLoyAAAAIBAJ&pg=1118,2513111 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Blue Holes of Andros |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1972|05|15}} |ProdCode=10 |ShortSummary=
:A visit to a deep network of underwater caves found offshore from the island of [[Andros, Bahamas|Andros]], with Dr. George Benjamin, a Canadian research chemist and the world's foremost authority on the Bahamas' "[[blue hole]]s" (underwater caves).<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=rG9kAAAAIBAJ&pg=3664%2C852232 |title=Program Highlights for the week |work=The Calgary Herald |date=May 12, 1972 |page=3, World of Television |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123654/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=rG9kAAAAIBAJ&pg=3664,852232 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=rG9kAAAAIBAJ&pg=2852%2C860860 |title=Nature of Things |work=The Calgary Herald |date=May 12, 1972 |page=5, World of Television |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123657/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=rG9kAAAAIBAJ&pg=2852,860860 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=woIuAAAAIBAJ&pg=6192%2C4859728 |title=HIGHLIGHTS This Week |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=May 13, 1972 |page=13, HIGHLIGHTS This Week |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123650/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=woIuAAAAIBAJ&pg=6192,4859728 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

