{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Puffins, Predators and Pirates |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1973|11|26}} |ProdCode=01 |ShortSummary=
:Season Premier: A biological study which reveals the plight of one of the world's last puffin colonies on Great Island off the eastern coast of Newfoundland.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=They Lead a Precarious Existence: Puffins |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=Nov 24, 1973 |page=24 TV/Times |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=TpMuAAAAIBAJ&pg=4793%2C2584231 |access-date=2016-03-20 |archive-date=2023-10-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123655/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=TpMuAAAAIBAJ&pg=4793,2584231 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Club of Rome|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1973|12|03}} |ProdCode=02 |ShortSummary=
:Our world is littered with the ruins of civilizations which have collapsed. A group of thinkers called [[Club of Rome|The Club of Rome]], thinks that we may be on the verge of chaos – social and political unrest, pollution, food and energy shortages – which could eventually reduce our civilization to ruins. The group is trying to find answers which will prevent our society from ruining itself.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/45897525/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=December 1, 1973 |page=20 |access-date=July 27, 2016 |archive-date=August 19, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160819062430/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/45897525/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Ellesmere Land|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1973|12|10}} |ProdCode=03 |ShortSummary=
:Summer comes to the [[Fosheim Peninsula]] of Ellesmere Island in Canada's vast high Arctic: giant furry musk oxen, jaegers cruising the valley skies, fox eating the eggs of a black bellied plover, droves of Arctic hares.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98170248/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=December 9, 1973 |page=35 |access-date=July 27, 2016 |archive-date=August 19, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160819045129/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98170248/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Anybody's Child|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1973|12|17}} |ProdCode=04 |ShortSummary=
:Michael is one of four youngsters living in a house. Each child suffers from severe emotional disturbances or mental illness, and in some cases, had been written off by society as untreatable. As an alternative to institutional treatment they are being brought up in a warm family environment by two young child care workers.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/45898955/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=December 15, 1973 |page=19 |access-date=July 27, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818100339/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/45898955/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Grouse Country|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1973|12|24}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:A look at grouse, one of the most plentiful birds in Canada; highly conspicuous, colorful and greatly admired by hunters and birdwatchers alike.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/45899666/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=December 22, 1973 |page=19 |access-date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818212140/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/45899666/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Vanishing Peoples: Lacandons|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1973|12|31}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:This special focuses on the Lacandons, direct descendants of the great Mayan civilizations. Isolated from modern society, the Lacandons have been able to preserve the Mayan philosophies which help them solve the problems of survival and fulfillment in the jungle.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98460301/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=December 30, 1973 |pages=26–27 |access-date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818223645/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98460301/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=A Comet's Tale |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|01|07}} |ProdCode=05 |ShortSummary=
:Czech astronomer [[Luboš Kohoutek|Dr. Luboš Kohoutek]], discoverer of the current heavenly phenomenon [[Comet Kohoutek]] 1973 f, is among the participants in this full-hour special. [[Roy Bonisteel]] is host of the program which examines comets from a scientific viewpoint, and heavenly signs and portents of doom from psychological and historical perspectives.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/68433263/ |title=tv week |work=The Brandon Sun |date=January 4, 1974}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The First Inch|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|01|14}} |ProdCode=06 |ShortSummary=
:What goes on in the very top layer of soil is often too small to see with the naked eye. When photographed under a microscope, that first inch of soil reveals itself to be one of the most vital of the life cycles affecting man. The tiny, invisible hordes of bacteria, plant eaters, parasites and predators are the subject of this program.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46014153/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=January 12, 1974 |page=20 |access-date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818212115/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46014153/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Serious Business of Play|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|01|21}} |ProdCode=07 |ShortSummary=
:Play is nature's method of learning about environment and about life for the young. This episode explores our world of play and its importance for survival.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98177907/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=January 20, 1974 |page=31 |access-date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818194638/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98177907/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Out of the Mouths of Babes|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|01|28}} |ProdCode=08 |ShortSummary=
:Little children learn languages, especially their own, with astonishing ease. Why this is so is the subject of this film.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46039996/ |title=TV Programs and Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=January 28, 1974 |page=26 |access-date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818121308/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46039996/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Joy of Effort|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|02|04}} |ProdCode=09 |ShortSummary=
:How the laws of physics are being applied to athletic endeavors, and coaches being taught how to use science rather than just "common sense" to help athletes get the most out of their bodies.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46452780/ |title=TV Programs and Highlights |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=February 4, 1974 |page=18 |access-date=July 30, 2016 |archive-date=August 19, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160819041059/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46452780/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Cree of Paint Hills|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|03|24}} |ProdCode=special |ShortSummary=
:A special documentary of the [[Cree]] inhabitants of Paint Hills, on the eastern shore of [[James Bay]] in Quebec.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=pANlAAAAIBAJ&pg=2670%2C778130 |title=TV Times |work=The Edmonton Journal |date=March 22, 1974 |page=8, TV Times |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123658/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=pANlAAAAIBAJ&pg=2670,778130 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=James Bay|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1974|03|28}} |ProdCode=special |ShortSummary=
:A 200-mile voyage up the [[La Grande River]], on the east coast of James Bay, showing the Indian settlement at Fort George.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46197840/ |title=TV Journal |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=March 23, 1974 |page=35 |access-date=July 30, 2016 |archive-date=August 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818101119/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/46197840/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

