{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Mendi |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1974|10|08}}|ProdCode=Special |ShortSummary=
:It was not until 1930 that the outside world knew that there were people living in the highlands of Papua, New Guinea. In 1950 the first contact was made with a group of 55,000 Mendi, part of a million inhabitants of the New Guinea highlands, formerly not known to exist. The Australians have since built an airstrip, a hospital, schools, a hotel and other permanent buildings there, but the Mendi have kept their culture intact. A CBC film crew directed by Nancy Archibald has recorded some of the ancient culture and lifestyle of the Mendi and the results are presented in this special one-hour documentary.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/68438452/ |title=Mendi culture documented |work=The Brandon Sun |date=October 4, 1974 |page=1, tv week section |access-date=October 7, 2016 |archive-date=October 9, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161009141803/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/68438452/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=And God Created Great Whales |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1974|10|09}} |ProdCode=01 |ShortSummary=
:A documentary showing the behaviour of killer whales in the wild, in the waters off Vancouver Island.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Lq4yAAAAIBAJ&pg=4329%2C2196588 |title=The Saturday Citizen TV &#124; Times |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=October 5, 1974 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123800/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Lq4yAAAAIBAJ&pg=4329,2196588 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

