{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Sable Island|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1977|02|02}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:The program focuses on a small island about 100 miles off Nova Scotia, where herds of wild horses live. Because they have been separated from the mainland for so long, the horses of Sable Island are considered a sub-species. The island is the breeding ground of the [[Savannah sparrow|Ipswich sparrow]] and the birthplace of the rare [[grey seal]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/68683450/ |title=TV Week |work=The Brandon Sun |date=January 28, 1977 |page=10 |access-date=August 21, 2016 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123702/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/68683450/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=When The Wind Blows|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1977|02|09}} |ProdCode=07 |ShortSummary=
:A look at the uses man has made of the wind, from sailboats to windmills to modern turbines for generating electricity.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=DHswAAAAIBAJ&pg=4205%2C1308545 |title=TV Times |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=February 5, 1977 |page=8 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123700/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=DHswAAAAIBAJ&pg=4205,1308545 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://collections.cinematheque.qc.ca/recherche/en/oeuvres/fiche/66885-when-the-wind-blows |title=When the Wind Blows |work=Cinémathèque québécoise |access-date=2016-08-22 |archive-date=2016-08-22 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160822180012/http://collections.cinematheque.qc.ca/recherche/en/oeuvres/fiche/66885-when-the-wind-blows |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Funk Island"; alternate title: "The Funks|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1977|02|16}} |ProdCode=08 |ShortSummary=
:Shows some of the species of seabirds to be found on Funk Island, situated 40 miles east of Newfoundland, which is a breeding ground of more than one million seabirds, and stresses the need for their protection against man.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=CjhVAAAAIBAJ&pg=1714%2C243803 |title=Tonight's television |work=The Leader-Post |location=Regina, Saskatchewan |date=February 16, 1977 |page=43 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123657/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=CjhVAAAAIBAJ&pg=1714,243803 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.bfi.org.uk/films-tv-people/4ce2b6d8e46c1 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160412075751/http://www.bfi.org.uk/films-tv-people/4ce2b6d8e46c1 |url-status=dead |archive-date=April 12, 2016 |title=The Nature of Things: The Funks (1978) |work=British Film Institute |access-date=2016-03-20}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=sDY0AAAAIBAJ&pg=2320%2C1365894 |title=CBC Television at its best |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=February 12, 1977 |page=12, TV Times |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123650/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=sDY0AAAAIBAJ&pg=2320,1365894 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

