{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Roger Tory Peterson: Portrait of a Birdwatcher |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1978|09|11}} |ProdCode=special |ShortSummary=
:Roger Tory Peterson revolutionized the science of ornithology by devising a system of bird identification based on his observation that each bird displays a unique set of markings. This profile follows the artist-naturalist into the fields and marshes of North America and Antarctica as he leads tours and displays some of the photographic techniques he uses for his field guides.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Marcovitz |first=Susan |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=xp8tAAAAIBAJ&pg=2240%2C3621897 |title=Highlights: Birdman of America on CBC |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=September 11, 1978 |page=49 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123657/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=xp8tAAAAIBAJ&pg=2240,3621897 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=s1tVAAAAIBAJ&pg=6062%2C2317074 |title=He wrote the bible on birds |work=The Leader-Post |location=Regina, Saskatchewan |date=September 8, 1978 |page=9, Television section |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123652/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=s1tVAAAAIBAJ&pg=6062,2317074 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

