{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Search|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1978|12|24}} |ProdCode=11 |ShortSummary=
:''The Search'' follows World Health Organization medical teams on their campaign to vaccinate the against smallpox in Somalia, the world's last location where the disease survives.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=6m5VAAAAIBAJ&pg=3504%2C1977277 |title=Television |work=The Leader-Post |location=Regina, Saskatchewan |date=December 22, 1978 |page=4 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123744/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=6m5VAAAAIBAJ&pg=3504,1977277 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Cajuns|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1978|12|31}} |ProdCode=12 |ShortSummary=
:The descendants of Nova Scotia's Acadians and their lifestyle are profiled at their adopted home, the Bayou Lafourche in southern Louisiana.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=725VAAAAIBAJ&pg=4881%2C3536283 |title=Television |work=The Leader-Post |location=Regina, Saskatchewan |date=December 29, 1978 |page=4 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123731/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=725VAAAAIBAJ&pg=4881,3536283 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Coming and Going|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1979|02|07}} |ProdCode=special |ShortSummary=
:New ways of dealing with the terminally ill are examined in ''Coming and Going'', a sensitive treatment of a serious problem. With the help of relatives and hospital staff, patients come to terms with their illness.<ref>{{cite journal |title=Coming and Going |journal=Cinema Canada |date=May 1979 |last=Lazer |first=Charles |issue=55 |page=37 |url=http://cinemacanada.athabascau.ca/index.php/cinema/article/viewFile/2256/2306 |format=PDF |access-date=2016-12-18 |archive-date=2020-08-03 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200803110514/http://cinemacanada.athabascau.ca/index.php/cinema/article/viewFile/2256/2306 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=45QuAAAAIBAJ&pg=7178%2C3437099 |title=TV TODAY |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=February 7, 1979 |page=31 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123752/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=45QuAAAAIBAJ&pg=7178,3437099 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}
