{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Mendi|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|01|09}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:A Stone Age tribe which left 50,000 members living off the land in Papua, New Guinea is examined.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Lb4yAAAAIBAJ&pg=7015%2C633982 |title=Television |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=January 9, 1980 |page=42 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123649/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Lb4yAAAAIBAJ&pg=7015,633982 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41537261/ |title=Television Listings |work=The Ottawa Journal |date=January 9, 1980 |access-date=December 24, 2016 |archive-date=December 24, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161224170835/https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/41537261/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Cree of Paint Hills|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|01|16}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:A feature on the Cree Indians of the eastern James Bay region and the threats of modern society to their lifestyle. This is a last minute change from ''Paul Jacobs and the Nuclear Gang'', the feature originally scheduled to appear at this time.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=TBYyAAAAIBAJ&pg=878%2C2882664 |title=TV Highlights |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=January 16, 1980 |page=60 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123702/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=TBYyAAAAIBAJ&pg=878,2882664 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Lacandons|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|01|23}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:A vanishing tribe of North American Indians in Mexico which is living according to the religious rites of past centuries is profiled.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Zh8yAAAAIBAJ&pg=4504%2C895550 |title=TV Highlights |work=The Montreal Gazette |date=January 23, 1980 |page=44 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123700/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=Zh8yAAAAIBAJ&pg=4504,895550 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=[[Paul Jacobs and the Nuclear Gang]]|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|02|06}} |ProdCode=12 |ShortSummary=
:For more than twenty years a freelance American journalist named [[Paul Jacobs (activist)|Paul Jacobs]] interviewed people exposed to nuclear fall-out from bomb tests in Nevada in an attempt to establish a link between such exposure and cancer. In this episode Jacobs' investigations are examined.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Musselwhite |first=Bill |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=G3VkAAAAIBAJ&pg=3601%2C750394 |title=Worth Watching |work=The Calgary Herald |date=February 1, 1980 |page=45, TV Times section |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123703/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=G3VkAAAAIBAJ&pg=3601,750394 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Roger Tory Peterson: Portrait of a Birdwatcher|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|02|13}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:The work of Peterson and his intense love of nature are examined in this documentary which shows him at work in his studio and at his Connecticut home.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=2HdVAAAAIBAJ&pg=4206%2C2203936 |title=Television |work=The Leader-Post |location=Regina, Saskatchewan |date=February 8, 1980 |page=10 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123654/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=2HdVAAAAIBAJ&pg=4206,2203936 |url-status=live }}</ref> }}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Crocodile City / Spanish Galleons / World's Largest Windmill / Cement|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|02|20}} |ProdCode=13 |ShortSummary=
:This magazine edition includes four segments: a look at [[Lamanai]] (Crocodile City), built by the Maya of Belize between 400 and 300 BC, as it was being excavated by [[David M. Pendergast|David Pendergast]] of the Royal Ontario Museum, assisted by other specialists and a work-force of direct descendants of the Maya; ''Spanish Galleons'': A look at the recent discovery and exploration of Spanish treasure ships wrecked off the coast of Texas four centuries ago, and techniques used in identifying encrusted objects; ''World's Largest Windmill'': Students and teachers of a Danish Folk School have built a windmill 75 meters high that produces 2,000 kilowatts of electricity, and ''Cement'': A look at the properties of cement.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=UXVkAAAAIBAJ&pg=4511%2C3254969 |title=TV Times |work=The Calgary Herald |date=February 15, 1980 |page=47 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123650/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=UXVkAAAAIBAJ&pg=4511,3254969 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=High altitude Physiology / The Vision of Galileo / Dust Storms|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|02|27}} |ProdCode=14 |ShortSummary=
:Technological developments involving man's survival at high altitudes; a look at the life of Galileo, Italian astronomer, mathematician and physicist, including recreation of some of his experiments; and an examination of the global meteorological effects of Sahara dust storms.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=A74yAAAAIBAJ&pg=6900%2C1290356 |title=Television |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=February 27, 1980 |page=80 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123650/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=A74yAAAAIBAJ&pg=6900,1290356 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Seal Psychology / Chiricahuas / Violins |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1980|03|05}} |ProdCode=15 |ShortSummary=
:''Seal Psychology'': A study of the ability of seals to navigate and catch fish in waters where it is too dark for the seals to see. ''[[Chiricahua Mountains|Chiricahuas]]'': A look at the Chiricahua mountains and their wildlife in southeast Arizona. ''Violins'': How violins are made, including an interview with a violin maker, and footage of students at the International School of Lute Making in Cremona, Italy.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=h_RlAAAAIBAJ&pg=983%2C2459374 |title=Television listings |work=The Edmonton Journal |date=March 5, 1980 |page=G4 |access-date=October 5, 2020 |archive-date=October 23, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023123704/https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=h_RlAAAAIBAJ&pg=983,2459374 |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

