{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Air Craft|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1985|10|16}} |ProdCode=02 |ShortSummary=
:A look at the machines designed to enable man to fly, from the Wright Brothers to today's revolutionary designs.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=iXdkAAAAIBAJ&pg=5557%2C679142 |title=TV Times |work=The Calgary Herald |date=October 11, 1985 |page=68}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99069794/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=October 13, 1985 |page=58}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Muscle Fibre / How Fish Swim|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1985|10|23}} |ProdCode=03 |ShortSummary=
:''Muscle Fibre'': An examination of the mechanics of muscle contraction, looking at the roles of slow and fast types of muscle fibres. ''How Fish Swim'': An examination of the biomechanics of fish locomotion, looking at the physical differences between different types of fish.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://pgnewspapers.pgpl.ca/fedora/repository/pgc:1985-10-23-18 |title=TV Schedule |work=The Citizen |location=Prince George, British Columbia |date=October 23, 1985 |page=18}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Open Heart|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1985|10|30}} |ProdCode=04 |ShortSummary=
:A profile of pioneering heart surgeon Dr. William Bigelow, focusing on the development of early heart surgery procedures.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://pgnewspapers.pgpl.ca/fedora/repository/pgc:1985-10-30-22 |title=TV Schedule |work=The Citizen |location=Prince George, British Columbia |date=October 30, 1985 |page=22}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99048079/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=October 27, 1985 |page=58}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Plant Communication / Jaipur Foot|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1985|11|06}} |ProdCode=05 |ShortSummary=
:''Plant Communication'': A look at the chemical defence mechanisms of plants and how they are triggered. [[Jaipur foot|''Jaipur Foot'']]: An artificial foot designed to fit in with rural India's environment and culture.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://pgnewspapers.pgpl.ca/fedora/repository/pgc:1985-11-06-18 |title=TV Schedule |work=The Citizen |location=Prince George, British Columbia |date=November 6, 1985 |page=18}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Doctors of Tomorrow / Walking / The Vortex |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1985|11|13}} |ProdCode=06 |ShortSummary=
:''Doctors of Tomorrow'': A unconventional form of medical education at [[McMaster University]], in a program of self-directed learning, with no classes, lectures, or exams. ''Walking'': An examination of the continual pendulum-like exchange of potential and kinetic energy that makes walking the most efficient form of human locomotion. ''The Vortex'': A description of how whirlpools are formed and the consequences of this primary pattern of movement on the surrounding environment.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/98990326/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=November 10, 1985 |page=62}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://pgnewspapers.pgpl.ca/fedora/repository/pgc:1985-11-13-18 |title=TV Schedule |work=The Citizen |location=Prince George, British Columbia |date=November 13, 1985 |page=18}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Dinosaurs: Remains to be Seen |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1985|11|20}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:Evidence from fossilized footprints, bones and pollen are used to create a facsimile of the world of the dinosaur.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99091586/ |title=The TV Book |work=Detroit Free Press |date=November 17, 1985 |page=62}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Ducks in Danger |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1985|11|27}} |ProdCode=07 |ShortSummary=
:David Suzuki investigates how the duck population is being threatened by toxic water, poor hunting regulations and blocked legislation.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://pgnewspapers.pgpl.ca/fedora/repository/pgc:1985-11-27-18 |title=TV Schedule |work=The Citizen |location=Prince George, British Columbia |date=November 27, 1985 |page=18}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/99055291/ |title=Of Special Interest |work=Detroit Free Press |date=November 24, 1985 |page=57, The TV Book}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The New Face of Leprosy |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1985|12|04}} |ProdCode=08 |ShortSummary=
:A progress report on leprosy includes programs designed to educate people in recognizing early symptoms of this disease that still afflicts people worldwide.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://pgnewspapers.pgpl.ca/fedora/repository/pgc:1985-12-04-24 |title=TV Schedule |work=The Citizen |location=Prince George, British Columbia |date=December 4, 1985 |page=24}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=How Alcohol Affects the Body / Ancient Life-forms / The Physics of Archery|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1985|12|11}} |ProdCode=??}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Islands at the Edge |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|01|29}} |ProdCode=?? |ShortSummary=
