== Season 27: 1986–1987 ==
{| class="wikitable plainrowheaders" style="width:100%; margin:auto;"
!Title!!width="140"|Broadcast date!!width="40"|Episode

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=Season Premier |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|10|08}} |ProdCode=01 |ShortSummary=
:David Suzuki is the host of this award-winning science show which begins its 27th season. What will the car of the future be like? Faster? Sleeker? Will it be built by humans – or machines? Will it continue to pollute and kill? Join David Suzuki for an eye-opening ride through the fact and fantasy of the machine we love. And hate.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=_QxlAAAAIBAJ&pg=6086%2C1961690 |title=TV Times |work=The Calgary Herald |date=October 3, 1986 |page=58, TV Times |access-date=2016-04-09}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=_QxlAAAAIBAJ&pg=5973%2C1952298 |title=Let's go for a spin in Next Year's Model |work=The Calgary Herald |date=October 3, 1986 |page=53, TV Times |access-date=2016-04-09}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=Restless Sky; Rotation; Handcraft in History |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|10|15}} |ProdCode=02 |ShortSummary=
:Clouds, and the atmospheric forces that create weather; an illustration of the principle of rotation; traditional methods and modern techniques employed in making paper in Nepal.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80511800/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=October 15, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-09}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.tvguide.com/celebrities/david-suzuki/credits/284030/284023/ |title=David Suzuki: Celebrity |work=TV Guide |access-date=2016-04-09}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=The Niagara Escarpment: A Rock Video |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|10|22}} |ProdCode=03 |ShortSummary=
:A look at the dangerous and beautiful Niagara Escarpment, a limestone spine that runs northward from Niagara Falls through the densely populated province of Ontario.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80511888/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=October 22, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-08}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://yclibw.yukoncollege.yk.ca/TLCScripts/interpac.dll?LabelDisplay&DataNumber=550277803&RecordNumber=29527&SearchAvailableOnly=0&FormId=2055369&ItemField=4&Config=ysm&Branch=,1 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160423013829/http://yclibw.yukoncollege.yk.ca/TLCScripts/interpac.dll?LabelDisplay&DataNumber=550277803&RecordNumber=29527&SearchAvailableOnly=0&FormId=2055369&ItemField=4&Config=ysm&Branch=,1 |url-status=dead |archive-date=April 23, 2016 |title=Yukon College Library Catalogue |work=Yukon College |access-date=2016-04-09 }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=(Placeholder) |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|10|29}} |ProdCode=04 |ShortSummary=
:Bereaved Argentinian women whose persistence and courage have enlisted help from American geneticists and forensic scientists in identifying the victims of their former government's persecution; ultrasonic sound and kidney stones; ambitious curbside recycling programs.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80511974/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=October 29, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-26}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=(Placeholder) |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|11|05}} |ProdCode=05 |ShortSummary=
:A look at the therapeutic use of plants over the years to cure illnesses and maintain good health, and how the deteriorating number of plant species in the world may prove to be a medical, as well as environmental, loss to humanity.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80512058/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=November 5, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-26}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=(Placeholder) |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|11|12}} |ProdCode=06 |ShortSummary=
:A look at how some animals, including the snapping shrimp and possibly the whale, use sound waves to stun their prey.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80512144/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=November 12, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-26}}</ref>}}

<!-- No episode on 11/19/1986 -->

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Women of Kerala / Vortex |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|11|26}} |ProdCode=07 |ShortSummary=
:Describes a program in Kerala, a state in southern India, where a combination of contraception, voluntary sterilization, increased education, a lowered rate of infant mortality, and the extension of health care to impoverished rural areas has produced a dramatic decrease in the birth rate. Also, scientific and technical research focused on the vortex.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80512379/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=November 26, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-26}}</ref><ref>{{cite book |title=Women of Kerala |isbn=9788126517824 |oclc=19979226 |last1=Walker |first1=Jearl |date=30 July 2008 |publisher=Wiley India Pvt. Limited }}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Air Craft |OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|1986|12|03}} |ProdCode=repeat |ShortSummary=
:A look at flying machines, from the Wright Brothers to today's revolutionary designs.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=http://theprogress.newspapers.com/image/80512497/ |title=Wednesday Highlights |work=The Chilliwack Progress |date=December 3, 1986 |page=D2 |access-date=2016-04-08}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Familiar Face of Love|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1986|12|10}} |ProdCode=08 |ShortSummary=
:An exploration into the psychological and social forces which form our ideas and feelings about the opposite sex.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=jcEyAAAAIBAJ&pg=1549%2C6077231 |title=What's on tonight |work=The Ottawa Citizen |date=December 10, 1986 |page=F18 |access-date=2016-03-28}}</ref><ref>{{cite book |last1=Coleman |first1=Eli |author-link=Eli Coleman |title=John Money: A Tribute |chapter=Bibliography |chapter-url=https://books.google.com/books?id=Be28xb4JPbwC&q=%22the+nature+of+things%22+%22The+Familiar+Face+of+Love%22&pg=PA175 |publisher=The Haworth Press, Inc. |year=1991 |page=175 |isbn=1-56024-190-X}}</ref>
}}

