:Three-quarters of a million hysterectomies are performed annually in North America. In close to 80% of these the ovaries are removed at the time of surgery, which robs women of a natural and healthy hormonal balance, and which can result in subsequent problems. This documentary looks at the choices being made and possible less-invasive alternatives.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/ |title=the nature of things |work=CBC |url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20051222020951/http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/ |archive-date=2005-12-22 |access-date=2016-05-05}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/show_hysterectomy.html |title=sex, lies and secrecy: dissecting hysterectomy |work=CBC |url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20040925040028/http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/show_hysterectomy.html |archive-date=2004-09-25 |access-date=2016-05-05}}</ref> }}

