{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Wasted|OriginalAirDate= {{Start date|2016|01|21}} |ProdCode=10 |ShortSummary=
:The personal story of a North Vancouver addictions therapist who himself battled alcoholism until he was homeless, and a search of evidence-based addiction treatments.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Spitale-Leisk |first=Maria |url=http://www.nsnews.com/news/couple-chronicles-addiction-struggles-1.2154733 |title=Couple chronicles addiction struggles |work=north shore news |location=Vancouver, British Columbia |date=January 20, 2016 |access-date=2016-04-19}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Call of the Baby Beluga|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|01|28}} |ProdCode=11 |ShortSummary=
:The film chronicles what happened when humans learned about the intricate social lives and customs of the endangered community of St. Lawrence whales and started to use their new knowledge and empathy to help them.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=McKenna |first=Barb |url=http://www.capebretonpost.com/News/Regional/2016-01-27/article-4416956/Nature-of-Things-to-feature-Liverpools-baby-beluga/1 |title=Nature of Things to feature Liverpool's baby beluga |work=Cape Breton Post |date=January 27, 2016 |access-date=2016-03-20}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Eagles Next Door|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|02|04}} |ProdCode=12 |ShortSummary=
:A breeding pair of bald eagles in the suburbs of Vancouver, Canada, is followed over the course of a year, and adaptations the eagles have made to be successful in the city are observed.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/episodes/eagles-next-door |title=Eagles Next Door |work=CBC/Radio-Canada |url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151205123931/http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/episodes/eagles-next-door |archive-date=2015-12-05 |access-date=2016-04-18}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Trapped in a Human Zoo|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|02|11}} |ProdCode=13 |ShortSummary=
:Based on the diaries of [[Abraham Ulrikab]], this is the story of the journey of eight Inuit who came from Labrador to Europe in 1880, lured by promises of adventures and wealth, only to realize they had been trapped in a world of human zoos. Thirty-five thousand indigenous people from around the world were recruited for these zoos.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/episodes/trapped-in-a-human-zoo |title=Trapped in a Human Zoo |work=CBC/Radio-Canada |url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160202030951/http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/episodes/trapped-in-a-human-zoo |archive-date=2016-02-02 |access-date=2016-04-18}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=Wolverine: Ghost of the Northern Forest|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|02|25}} |ProdCode=14 |ShortSummary=
:''Wolverine: Ghost of the Northern Forest'' recounts the fascinating story of Canadian wildlife filmmaker Andrew Manske's relentless, five-year quest to find and film the legendary and elusive wolverine.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Griwkowsky |first=Fish |url=https://edmontonjournal.com/entertainment/television/alberta-filmmaker-advances-understanding-of-wolverines |title=Alberta filmmaker advances understanding of wolverines |work=Edmonton Journal |date=February 21, 2016 |access-date=2016-04-17}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=The Equalizer|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|03|03}} |ProdCode=15 |ShortSummary=
:Investigate how modern science and technology help athletes achieve new peaks of human performance.<ref name="OntarioScienceCentre-2015-Sep">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.ontariosciencecentre.ca/Media/Details/417/ |title=Ontario Science Centre presents exclusive documentary previews of CBC-TV's The Nature of Things to encourage dialogue about science |work=Ontario Science Centre |date=2015-09-29 |access-date=2016-03-20}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=While You Were Sleeping (The Science of Sleep)|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|03|10}} |ProdCode=16 |ShortSummary=
:Dr. [[Jennifer Gardy]] discusses the world of sleep.<ref name="natureofthings/while-sleeping">{{#invoke:cite|web|title=What Happens in Your Brain While You Sleep? New Research |url=http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/episodes/while-your-were-sleeping |website=The Nature of Things |publisher=CBC-TV |access-date=3 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160208121048/http://www.cbc.ca/natureofthings/episodes/while-your-were-sleeping |archive-date=8 February 2016}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list|Title=My Brain Made Me Do It|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|03|17}} |ProdCode=17 |ShortSummary=
:A study of how the biology of the brain influences criminal behaviour.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Friesen |first=Laura |url=http://www.nsi-canada.ca/2016/03/new-doc-from-merit-motion-pictures-premieres-tomorrow-on-cbc/ |title=New doc from Merit Motion Pictures premieres tomorrow on CBC |work=National Screen Institute – Canada |date=March 16, 2016 |access-date=2016-03-28}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=Suzuki@80 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|03|24}} |ProdCode=18 |ShortSummary=
:On David Suzuki's 80th birthday, ''The Nature of Things'' looks at his work as a scientist, environmental activist and television host.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Lederman |first=Marsha |url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/television/cbc-to-air-special-documentary-on-david-suzuki-for-his-80th-birthday/article29334925/ |title=CBC to air special documentary on David Suzuki for his 80th birthday. |work=The Globe and Mail |location=Canada |date=Mar 22, 2016 |access-date=2016-03-24}}</ref>}}

{{#invoke:Episode list|list |Title=Pets, Vets and Debts |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2016|03|31}} |ProdCode=19 |ShortSummary=
:Keeping pets healthy has grown into a billion dollar industry.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Nasmith |first=Cecilia |url=http://www.northumberlandtoday.com/2016/03/15/even-the-love-of-a-pet-is-not-cheap |title=Even the love of a pet is not cheap |work=Northumberland Today |location=Canada |date=March 15, 2016 |access-date=2016-03-23}}</ref>}}

